\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {8}{\ignorespaces Scalability validation across 800, 1{,}600, and 3{,}200 clients. Left: replica targeting --- achieved peak replicas (blue) track the expected $\lceil N/T \rceil $ (dashed) with a consistent $+2$ overshoot. Centre: scale-up reaction time increases modestly from 66~s to 86~s at $4\times $ the baseline client count. Right: achieved peak connections (red) meet or exceed the attempted count at all scales, confirming no OS-level TCP bottleneck for the WebSocket workload in the Kind environment.}}{13}{}\protected@file@percent }
